# Caches Cut Findings
#
# Distilled findings from the review, the understand pass, the ontology panel, and the design studies. Extend by adding keyed findings with a status and a link to evidence.

#>caches_cut_findings
#:layer #!pragmatics

^["extend"]{
 how: "add one key per finding inside the right frame: a statement string, then status and evidence on following keys; never rewrite another agent finding, add a counter instead"
 status_words: #[ verified, reported, proposed, open ]
 evidence: "link a file under ./references or a repo path with line numbers in the statement"
}

^["review"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/review/scorecard.md"
 accuracy: "core topic lists ran about 85 to 90 percent accurate; errors clustered in taste and wonder layers, which also carried invented effect sizes"
 harms: "physiology and nursing files carried clinical errors (liver in pregnancy, MTHFR and folic acid, vancomycin troughs, chlorhexidine oral care, nitroglycerin contraindications); quarantined in .spw/caches/index.spw"
 strongest: "film chemistry and optics, economics, linguistics, library science, molecular biology, the materials set, podcasting year rows"
 template: "version B (wonder_probes wrapper, dense key and formula facets) outperformed version A (leaf taste, bare wonder, invented percentages)"
 status: #verified
}

^["linking"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/linking.md"
 device: "anchors are the only intra-file addresses the seed resolves; ~path#anchor plus bias edges ={ } are the Spw-native link; expand transcludes bias edges"
 lsp_line: "LSP go-to-definition on ~path#anchor lands on line 1 because the fragment stays on the resolved path (navigation.ts); fixed in the fragnav patch"
 graph: "spw graph and census keep fragments in node ids and mint @alias pseudo-hubs; the caches taste hub had in-degree 60 from dispatch tables; fixed in the graphfrag patch"
 roots: "@roots are file-scoped; parent index roots do not reach children; bare @alias values are not links"
 forms: "~<tag> and ~< quoted > path forms are not PathRefs in the parser (394 and 157 canon uses)"
 status: #verified
}

^["measures"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/metrics.md"
 parse: "$% parses as a bare $ operation and a sibling % operation; only the first arm of %[a, b] is measured at runtime"
 binding: "handles bind only to 16 hover glossary names or .spw/state/observable.spw; the measure-context loader reads nothing from Spw source (frameLabel misses Parameter nodes)"
 cut_design: "world quantities live once as %ns.key{ value unit at rel src status } registry cells; surfaces cite them; reflexive handles stay within what census and form compute"
 status: #verified
}

^["tags"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/tags.md"
 indexed: "only #> anchors, same-line #:k #!v pairs, ~#name traits, flush #tags, and ##> are indexed by the LSP; #[ ] sets and ~#name() appositions are not"
 monotony: "the raw shelf had #:layer #!pragmatics on every file and single-use lenses and handles; tags carry information only when some but not all files share a value"
 valence: "canon makes valence charge-neutral material quality; catalog.ts and autocompletion conventions define it as outcome status; the palette paints bane as error red"
 status: #verified
}

^["lens"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/lens_lsp.md"
 gap: "the parser builds an Annotation with an apposition body for ~#lens(x); the LSP index, wonder hover, and inlay never read it; canon migrated toward ~#lens() while the LSP still reads // lens:"
 fix: "lens patch indexes APPOSITION tokens, reads lenses with precedence apposition then datum then comment, paints bodies as strings; hardening extracts hover code to handlers/wonder.ts"
 status: #verified
}

^["publishing"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/emit_bundle.md"
 emit: "emit reads one file, never follows includes, and flattens repeated keys last-write-wins; a ^emit frame scopes extraction; the brief host renders title, goal, audience, claim, proof, door, taste, acceptance"
 leak: "emit ir writes an absolute sourcePath; make it repo-relative before publishing packs"
 bundling: "expand is the working bundler: bias edges with fragments project the anchored node"
 status: #verified
}

^["clustering"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/ocean_cluster.md"
 ocean: "ocean names five things: a biome directory, a metaphor atlas, a runtime stability channel and dialect, a cache-tier contract, and an unimplemented cluster algorithm; only the metaphor and cluster layers are replaceable"
 hybrid: "authored tree, closed-vocabulary facets, authored typed edges, and computed clusters as prompts; plan-index.ts is the precedent"
 status: #verified
}

^["syntax"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/syntax_breadth.md"
 degrade: "valence words as keys, comparisons inside brackets, and bare tagged paths degrade or detach"
 swallow: "a medial capsule like 48<hours> and an empty binding take the next line; a #tag value followed by a key on the same line nests that key"
 validator: "spw-syntax-validate reports success when lexer errors exist; gates must read parse errors directly"
 architectures: "nine verified skeletons: timeline ladder, prerequisite DAG, comparison matrix, state machine, cadence schedule, claim ledger, glossary lattice, case dossier, probe battery"
 status: #verified
}

^["editors"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/understand/plugin_theory.md"
 defects: "VS Code cacheReflection drops layers; spw.trace.server is inert; IntelliJ folding treats # as a comment; commenter and language configuration disagree; spellcheck off; gutter markers have no navigation; previews open as dirty untitled documents"
 stale: ".spw/tooling/vscode-spw.spw:22 startup ladder and :46 projections section contradict README:28 and workspace-tree.ts"
 status: #verified
}

^["rendering"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/studies/render-synthesis.md"
 layers: "TextMate, LSP semantic tokens, and VS Code decorations are all regex; none reads the parser; claim status is invisible in every layer"
 palette: "23 color ids collapse to 13 hexes; bane is error red against charge-neutral canon; two light-mode colors fail WCAG contrast; anchor and intent nearly merge under deuteranopia"
 plain_text: "the cut is legible without color: one-space indent per depth, anchors at boundaries, one claim per line, about 4 seconds aloud per median statement"
 cli: "the CLI is already the monochrome environment with check, compare, and plan verbs; it lacks a predict slot; 24 ranked ergonomic changes, led by fragment-aware census, parseable cards, filled next steps, and a richer outline"
 voice: "cold_open say lines, reader marginalia as appositions promoted by recurrence, ^[arc] frames with clocks and prediction steps, and recipes now live in the contract"
 refused: "spw tour as onboarding is refused by the owner resume note; arrival is one fragment door"
 research: "highlighting shows small or null comprehension effects and a steady preference; monochrome practice rests on generation and pretesting, not difficulty"
 status: #verified
}

^["tokens_ast"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/studies/tokens-synthesis.md"
 errors_silent: "lexer errors land in parse().errors while success stays true, so the LSP publishes no diagnostic and spw-syntax-validate passes the file; the cut gate reads errors directly"
 events_cost: "the default trace event policy retains about 88 thousand events per edit for a 701-line file that the LSP never reads"
 dialect_spans: "dialect preprocessing joins lines, so token offsets stop matching source bytes under Spw.l and Spw.q pragmas"
 layers: "four coloring layers (two TextMate copies, regex semantic tokens, regex decorations) and none derives from the seed"
 design: "one RoleSpan stream from the cached parse, encoded by the LSP into a wire legend; practice modes, say lines, arcs, and dialect lowerings become filters or lowerings over it, each derived byte pointing at its source"
 first_moves: "publish parse errors regardless of success; parse once with path and a diagnostics event policy; make # prose consume to end of line in semantic tokens; add a seed tokenRoles function"
 same_line_law: "capsules, empty bindings, inline # comments, and valence chains each treat a line break differently; a valence-only value captures the next line operation"
 planned_surfaces: "spw/tokens-and-roles, spw/practice-modes, spw/transforms, spw/arcs-and-readings, spw/dialects-and-play, spw/lineage, and a code-and-canon source registry"
 status: #verified
}

^["persona"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/studies/persona-synthesis.json"
 evaluations: ~"./references/studies/persona.md"
 clusters: "twelve practitioner clusters: C-family programmers, physics, designers, mathematicians, engineers and chemists, life and clinical, linguists, social scientists, librarians, production crews, creators and streamers, educators and community"
 false_friends: "the most consequential collisions: comparison-shaped glyphs, numbers as people type them, a colon inside a value, the # family, = as assignment or equation, spaced infix that grabs neighbors, line-end capsules and empty keys, valence words read as merit, @ as mention or citation, and typographic or non-ASCII characters outside strings"
 rule_of_thumb: "most collisions fail silently; quote whatever you would read aloud"
 keyboards: "the familiarity matrix records each sigil per layout: dead keys on US-International, German, and French for ^ and ~, AltGr reach for ~ and # on several European layouts, and screen readers that announce # as number"
 contraptions: "nineteen exploration contraptions, from a false-friend collider and a dimension and conservation bench to a phase walker, a Mendeleev gap finder, a schedule order counter, a symmetry registry, and an interlinear gloss aligner"
 clustering_entrances: "concept hubs (conservation, symmetry, scaling and dimension, phase and transition, order and schedule, sign and feedback, gaps and prediction) gather anchors from at least two classes for readers who cluster conceptually"
 doors: "one fragment door per field plus a shared first hour; a door routes, it does not tour"
 status: #verified
}

^["panel"]{
 evidence: ~"./references/panel/verdicts.json"
 winner: "Colon or faceted archive, chosen by all three judges, with grafts from Workshop and Propaedia"
 grafts: "season hub, case dossiers, market hooks, Foxfire kits, streamers bench, engineering math core, canonical cores, replication and guideline ledgers, registry indexes, depth four where real"
 status: #verified
}

^["open_questions"]{
 lens_kind: "rename the LSP #: kind from lens to case so lens means only the reading"
 dollar_percent: "fuse $% into one token, or drop $ from canon"
 status_aim: "use #! mood for epistemic status, or register a claim case vocabulary"
 valence_source: "settle valence semantics between valence-architecture canon and catalog.ts"
 anchor_scope: "should an anchor bind the rest of its container, and should a file anchor address the whole surface"
 roots_inheritance: "should index roots reach children"
 bias_labels: "which bias labels transclude and which only point"
 same_line_law: "one rule for line boundaries across capsules, bindings, tags, and valence chains"
}
